# 1. MISSION

LEAN-1 focused on simplifying Student declarations.

LEAN-2 must now make reviewing those declarations equally straightforward.

The customer has repeatedly compared the current 5TOT interface against the Central Youth Union's online award selection systems.

Although the current 5TOT interface looks modern, its operational UX has become unnecessarily complicated.

Current problems include:

- Excessive intermediate review statuses.
- Too many separate review actions.
- Criterion-by-criterion navigation.
- Large floating review toolbars.
- Separate evidence approval controls.
- Redundant review completion buttons.
- Confusing review progress.
- Excessive nested cards.
- Poor utilization of desktop screen space.
- Review actions far away from the declaration being assessed.
- Too many overlapping panels.
- Responsive layout problems.
- AI-style technical wording.

The customer wants a LEAN review workflow.

**A reviewer opens the dossier, reads the Student declaration, inspects supporting evidence, clicks Đạt or Không đạt, and continues to the next declaration.**

No unnecessary wizard.

No forced navigation.

No artificial review steps.

No multiple confirmations for the same assessment.

Preserve a professional, premium and responsive interface.

**LEAN-2 MUST IMPLEMENT THIS EXPERIENCE IN ACTUAL PRODUCTION SOURCE CODE.**

