# 11. ALL_REQUIRED / AT_LEAST_N / ONE_OF

Correct eligibility aggregation is a primary acceptance gate.

## ALL_REQUIRED

Every mandatory child requirement must be satisfied.

However, whether a child requirement is satisfied must follow its own actual rule.

If a child requirement permits multiple declarations and needs one qualifying achievement:

- Declaration A: Pass.
- Declaration B: Fail.

The child requirement may still Pass because A satisfies it.

Do not fail the entire group merely because an additional declaration failed.

## AT_LEAST_N

Count the correct approved qualification unit:

- Distinct requirements.
- Distinct accepted alternatives.
- Valid achievements.

Use whichever counting model the actual regulation and canonical criteria define.

Do not double-count multiple declarations under one requirement when the rule requires distinct conditions.

## ONE_OF

One qualifying alternative may be sufficient.

If the Student submits only one qualifying alternative, do not demand assessments on unused alternatives.

## Multiple voluntary declarations

Preserve all additional declarations.

Do not mark them automatically Pass.

Do not delete or suppress evidence.

Distinguish minimum condition satisfaction from unresolved judgments on additional submitted items, according to the verified business completion contract.

## Conclusive Fail

Do not treat lack of a Pass as automatically equivalent to a confirmed Fail.

A requirement becomes conclusively failed only where the approved rules and available human judgments justify that result.

Write targeted unit tests for:

- Unreviewed.
- Partial review.
- Complete Pass.
- Complete Fail.
- One accepted declaration among failures.
- Optional alternatives not submitted.
- Multiple submissions under one form.
- Pending supplement.
- Supplement returned.
- Corrected human judgment.

