# 33. DEFINITION OF DONE

LEAN-2 is complete only when:

- A reviewer sees the five criteria as one clear continuous dossier.
- The Student's declarations are readable without excessive navigation.
- Evidence is accessible beside the declaration.
- Pass/Fail actions are direct and contextual.
- Human judgments persist through actual backend contracts in Real Mode, where authorized testing is available.
- Review progress is separate from eligibility.
- Fully reviewed failing applications are correctly representable.
- ONE_OF and ALL_REQUIRED work correctly.
- Redundant review controls are removed only after verifying their domain semantics.
- School and City judgments remain independent.
- School recommendations and Committee decisions are not automatically triggered.
- Student-submitted content stays protected.
- Desktop and mobile layouts are usable.
- Relevant tests pass.
- Any unavailable Real Mode verification is transparently reported.

Do not mark LEAN-2 fully PASS solely because the Demo UI looks correct.

